---
// About (English). French twin: src/pages/fr/about.astro.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import AuthorCard from '../components/content/AuthorCard.astro';
import NewsletterNote from '../components/content/NewsletterNote.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description="René Cotton makes Synaptane. Why he built a team second brain that stays in your own Git repository.">
  <PageHeader title="About" intro="Who makes Synaptane, and why." />
  <div class="container about">
    <AuthorCard lang="en" />
    <div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I'm René Cotton, and I make Synaptane. I built it for three reasons.
        </p>
        <h2>Knowledge gets lost</h2>
        <p>
          Every day, I explain things to AI assistants: the context of a decision, how a system works, what we tried
          and why it did not work. The answers are useful, and they disappear when the conversation ends. The wiki that
          should keep them is never up to date, because nobody has the time to maintain it.
        </p>
        <h2>A growing team needs to share what it knows</h2>
        <p>
          I run a company, and its team keeps growing. Each new person needs what the others already know, and the
          people who know it are often the busiest. I wanted that knowledge to circulate without asking anyone to
          become a documentation writer: you tell your assistant, and it ends up in the right page.
        </p>
        <h2>Your data stays with you</h2>
        <p>
          The memory of a team is too important to sit in a closed SaaS, in a format you cannot take back. With
          Synaptane, it is Markdown pages and your original files, PDFs, slides or scans, in your own Git repository: you can read it without Synaptane, back it up
          like any repository, and leave whenever you want. That is also why Synaptane is self-hosted and open source,
          under the Apache 2.0 license.
        </p>
        <p>
          I develop Synaptane with the help of AI coding assistants, and I review every change.
        </p>
        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          There is no email address: questions, ideas and feedback go to{' '}
          <a href={SITE.discussions}>GitHub Discussions</a>, where the answers help everyone. Bugs go to{' '}
          <a href={`${SITE.github}/issues`}>issues</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Security vulnerabilities: report them privately, never in a public issue. See{' '}
          <a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}>SECURITY.md</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <NewsletterNote title="A weekly newsletter on AI, in French" linkLabel="Read it on rene-cotton.fr">
        Every week, I write about artificial intelligence: what changes, and what it means in practice.
      </NewsletterNote>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-8); }
  }
  .prose h2:first-of-type { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
</style>
